      "math_academy_id": "e-4012",
      "problem": "The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below. Which of the following is true when $x\\rightarrow 2?$   \n\nI. $f(x) \\rightarrow  \\infty$\n\nII. $f(x) \\rightarrow  2$\n\nIII. $f(x) \\rightarrow  -\\infty$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/33650d66a0f3a2fae762b1c19da952597740868b00eeec11a14ad822536962e8.png)",
      "worked_solution": "From the given graph, we see that as $x$ approaches $2,$ the values of $f(x)$ increase, approaching $\\infty.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/4585f983dac68f3ac655fbaaed6481cd1479c4cffae2c10d9f08d991c6533f51.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
